WEBVTT

00:00:17.200 --> 00:00:19.330
How is Kanata doing?

00:00:19.330 --> 00:00:22.540
We don't have any anesthetics,
so I had to operate without them.

00:00:22.540 --> 00:00:25.370
It's incredible how he tolerated the pain.

00:00:25.370 --> 00:00:28.290
I have nothing but respect for him...

00:00:28.290 --> 00:00:30.370
He's stable now, in bed.

00:00:30.370 --> 00:00:31.790
I see...

00:00:31.790 --> 00:00:33.330
So his arm is...?

00:00:33.330 --> 00:00:36.330
Of course, there's no way to get it back.

00:00:36.330 --> 00:00:39.750
I'm sure someone will buy him
a good prosthetic, though.

00:00:39.750 --> 00:00:42.120
Right, your majesty?

00:00:42.120 --> 00:00:44.450
Stop being mean.

00:00:44.450 --> 00:00:46.500
I'm being as gentle as I can.

00:00:46.500 --> 00:00:49.790
I do sympathize with Charce's upbringing.

00:00:49.790 --> 00:00:53.750
But thinking about Kanata...

00:00:53.750 --> 00:00:57.290
Zack, you need to lock me up.

00:00:57.290 --> 00:01:01.330
Then, when you get to Astra,
you can send me to the police,

00:01:01.330 --> 00:01:04.120
along with the originals who made us clones.

00:01:04.120 --> 00:01:05.500
Charce...

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:10.500
There's no need for that.

00:01:10.500 --> 00:01:11.750
Kanata?!

00:01:12.580 --> 00:01:13.540
Kanata!

00:01:13.540 --> 00:01:14.750
You need to be asleep!

00:01:14.750 --> 00:01:19.660
It hurts too much! Also, I'm lonely...

00:01:19.660 --> 00:01:24.000
Charce, I'm not holding
any grudges against you.

00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:26.950
I acted on choices that I made by myself.

00:01:26.950 --> 00:01:31.200
If you hadn't shut down the sphere
when you did, I would be dead.

00:01:31.200 --> 00:01:33.160
Thanks for that.

00:01:33.160 --> 00:01:38.700
If we explain what happened, you won't
be charged. We'll make sure of it.

00:01:38.700 --> 00:01:41.120
That's why you need to make the choice, too.

00:01:41.120 --> 00:01:43.620
To live for yourself from now on.

00:01:45.500 --> 00:01:47.410
So you're going to trust him?

00:01:47.410 --> 00:01:48.950
I trust him.

00:01:48.950 --> 00:01:50.330
If he brings out another sphere?

00:01:50.330 --> 00:01:53.250
Then he can take my left arm, too!

00:01:53.250 --> 00:01:57.750
Why would we <i>not </i>trust him now?!
Was this whole trip a big lie?

00:01:57.750 --> 00:02:01.620
Everything stays as it was!
If anyone has a problem with that,

00:02:01.620 --> 00:02:04.040
we'll go one-on-one! I can take you
all on with one arm!

00:02:04.040 --> 00:02:07.000
One-on-one with what...?

00:02:07.000 --> 00:02:10.870
There's no problem. Just wanted
to hear it from you, Captain.

00:02:10.870 --> 00:02:16.040
Nobody on this team wants
to leave anybody out.

00:02:16.040 --> 00:02:19.910
Got it? You'll need to work hard...

00:02:19.910 --> 00:02:21.830
...to cover for Kanata.

00:02:23.040 --> 00:02:26.580
I'm truly sorry, everyone.

00:02:26.580 --> 00:02:30.290
Thanks to you, I am myself now.

00:02:30.290 --> 00:02:34.120
I want to live as my own original now.

00:02:34.120 --> 00:02:36.830
I want to go home with you all.

00:02:36.830 --> 00:02:39.370
Yes, of course.

00:02:39.370 --> 00:02:43.870
Besides, we have more questions to ask.

00:02:43.870 --> 00:02:45.870
I know.

00:02:45.870 --> 00:02:50.040
I'll tell you everything I know.

00:02:50.040 --> 00:02:52.450
The truth as recorded in Vixia.

00:02:52.750 --> 00:02:53.370
"Gloom"

00:02:53.370 --> 00:02:54.870
"Gloom"
Huh?!

00:02:54.870 --> 00:02:55.750
My arm hurts.

00:02:55.750 --> 00:02:57.160
Of course!

00:02:57.160 --> 00:02:58.000
Kanata!

00:02:58.000 --> 00:02:59.040
Also, I feel dizzy.

00:02:59.040 --> 00:03:02.830
Again, of course! How much blood
do you think you've lost?!

00:03:02.830 --> 00:03:06.700
Kanata needs to rest now.
The important talks will have to wait.

00:03:06.700 --> 00:03:08.410
Yes. I understand.

00:03:08.410 --> 00:03:12.080
All right guys. The rest of us
will start foraging tomorrow.

00:03:12.080 --> 00:03:13.830
Aye, yeah!

00:03:13.830 --> 00:03:14.870
Aye, yeah...

00:03:14.870 --> 00:03:16.450
You rest!

00:03:18.500 --> 00:03:19.540
"Planet Galem
Day 117 of being lost in space"

00:03:19.540 --> 00:03:23.950
"Planet Galem
Day 117 of being lost in space"
Team B5 camp log.
Day seven on Planet Galem.

00:03:23.950 --> 00:03:29.750
Fortunately, planet Galem is rich in food
and water, with a stable climate.

00:03:29.750 --> 00:03:32.700
Food collection is progressing steadily.

00:03:33.660 --> 00:03:41.000
Kanata is concentrating on nourishment
and sleep to recover from his injury.

00:03:41.000 --> 00:03:42.700
Hmm?

00:03:42.700 --> 00:03:43.750
I feel a little bad for Kanata,
who seems very bored.

00:03:43.750 --> 00:03:48.000
"Mind-numbingly boring game made by Zack"
I feel a little bad for Kanata,
who seems very bored.

00:03:50.120 --> 00:03:54.870
So I visited him many times to chat.

00:03:56.580 --> 00:04:01.700
So many shiny things everywhere.
This planet is very pretty.

00:04:01.700 --> 00:04:05.790
Yeah, it's a sight unlike anywhere else.

00:04:05.790 --> 00:04:12.620
I'll never forget this. The sights
and the time we spent together.

00:04:13.910 --> 00:04:16.000
Yeah, thanks to your photographic memory.

00:04:16.000 --> 00:04:18.080
That's not what I mean!

00:04:18.080 --> 00:04:19.700
It's a feelings thing.

00:04:19.700 --> 00:04:22.700
Yeah... I get it, I do.

00:04:22.700 --> 00:04:28.000
I feel the same way. All of this was
a super precious experience.

00:04:28.000 --> 00:04:31.410
Though we did go through some
rough times, too, of course.

00:04:37.330 --> 00:04:39.750
How is your arm?

00:04:39.750 --> 00:04:43.870
It hurts super bad, but I can manage.
I need to toughen up and get used to the pain.

00:04:43.870 --> 00:04:44.950
You're going to touch it up?

00:04:44.950 --> 00:04:47.950
That's not what I said!
Please don't touch the wound!

00:04:51.120 --> 00:04:57.120
Despite it all, I do wish this trip
would last just a bit longer.

00:04:57.120 --> 00:05:00.330
I am slightly sad that it's ending.

00:05:04.330 --> 00:05:05.290
"Planet Galem
Day 120 of being lost in space"

00:05:05.290 --> 00:05:07.660
"Planet Galem
Day 120 of being lost in space"
And finally, we gathered
enough food to depart this planet!

00:05:07.660 --> 00:05:12.040
And finally, we gathered
enough food to depart this planet!

00:05:12.040 --> 00:05:13.000
Good!

00:05:13.000 --> 00:05:14.120
Everyone ready?

00:05:14.120 --> 00:05:18.500
That was a really close call,
when the burr-burr attacked.

00:05:18.500 --> 00:05:22.700
Who would have thought the dullfish's
tentacles would be so useful?

00:05:22.700 --> 00:05:26.000
Did you know? The purple mandala
flower smells super bad!

00:05:26.000 --> 00:05:28.660
Thanks, I feel super left out!

00:05:30.410 --> 00:05:33.370
What are you laughing about?!
That noise you're making is a laugh, right?

00:05:42.870 --> 00:05:47.080
The next time we touch down, it's going
to be on a spaceport on Astra, isn't it?

00:05:47.080 --> 00:05:49.160
If we make it back safely.

00:05:49.160 --> 00:05:55.330
If our originals find out that we're alive,
they'll try to do something for sure.

00:05:55.330 --> 00:05:59.290
Quite possible. We should prepare somehow.

00:05:59.290 --> 00:06:02.370
Let's hear from Charce first.

00:06:08.450 --> 00:06:11.410
Entering faster-than-light travel.

00:06:11.410 --> 00:06:14.160
Destination: Planet Astra!

00:06:21.410 --> 00:06:23.250
Okay...

00:06:23.250 --> 00:06:27.040
We're all here. We have plenty of time.

00:06:27.040 --> 00:06:30.580
Can you tell us now, Charce? Take your time.

00:06:30.580 --> 00:06:31.620
Yes.

00:06:32.700 --> 00:06:37.290
I will now tell you the secret of Astra.

00:06:37.290 --> 00:06:41.410
In the past, there was a planet called Earth.

00:06:41.410 --> 00:06:49.120
In order to escape extinction by asteroid,
humanity chose to relocate to a new planet.

00:06:49.120 --> 00:06:54.950
Per Astra, Ad Astra. Overcome hardships to reach
the destination. That was the slogan.

00:06:54.950 --> 00:07:00.540
Humanity worked together to find
a new planet to move to.

00:07:00.540 --> 00:07:06.580
Two years later, almost miraculously,
a planet similar to Earth was found.

00:07:06.580 --> 00:07:11.910
The planet, 5,000 light years away,
was named Astra.

00:07:14.620 --> 00:07:17.910
That's in line with what Polina taught us.

00:07:17.910 --> 00:07:19.160
The issue is...

00:07:19.160 --> 00:07:23.580
Why weren't we aware of such
an important part of history?

00:07:23.580 --> 00:07:28.410
That's the secret of our world.
Only a few high-ranking government officials

00:07:28.410 --> 00:07:31.080
and the King of Vixia know the secret.

00:07:31.080 --> 00:07:35.290
The Vixia Royal Quarter was built
to safeguard that secret.

00:07:35.290 --> 00:07:37.950
That's why it's such an enclosed environment.

00:07:37.950 --> 00:07:41.910
The secret is passed on from king to king.

00:07:41.910 --> 00:07:47.370
Of course, the current king
had plans to remain king forever.

00:07:47.370 --> 00:07:53.290
So you mean there are historical facts
that we don't know, right?

00:07:53.290 --> 00:07:56.080
The history you know has been
warped from the truth.

00:07:56.080 --> 00:07:59.580
But it was all done in the name of peace.

00:08:01.080 --> 00:08:06.700
The artificial wormhole was key to making
this huge immigration project possible.

00:08:06.700 --> 00:08:09.370
Gates were built all over the world.

00:08:09.370 --> 00:08:13.540
Over 10,000 tunnels
connected Earth and Astra.

00:08:15.580 --> 00:08:22.620
Creating cities out of nothing was a huge
undertaking. Work was extremely difficult.

00:08:22.620 --> 00:08:27.040
But since existing technologies could be
transported via wormhole,

00:08:27.040 --> 00:08:29.660
the process got faster and faster.

00:08:30.910 --> 00:08:37.160
Meanwhile on Earth, the immigration project
was revealed to the entire world.

00:08:37.160 --> 00:08:42.410
People were confused, panicked, and...

00:08:42.410 --> 00:08:48.660
...they began to fight over land
ownership in the new world.

00:08:48.660 --> 00:08:53.080
Race, religion, international power relations...

00:08:53.080 --> 00:08:58.450
It became the trigger to make all
of humanity's problems explode.

00:08:58.450 --> 00:09:05.200
In just two months during 2052, half of
the entire population of humanity was lost.

00:09:05.200 --> 00:09:08.040
It was that bad?

00:09:08.040 --> 00:09:11.830
The wormholes helped make everything worse.

00:09:11.830 --> 00:09:15.620
Think about it. It allows you to travel
to another location, instantly.

00:09:15.620 --> 00:09:18.950
It made all terrorist attacks and
assassinations easy to pull off.

00:09:18.950 --> 00:09:22.250
They weren't built for that...

00:09:22.250 --> 00:09:27.200
The same thing is seen
throughout human history.

00:09:27.200 --> 00:09:32.160
We build it first, before being afraid. Always.

00:09:32.160 --> 00:09:37.830
The survivors of the war regretted
the foolishness and vowed to create peace.

00:09:37.830 --> 00:09:43.620
Nations were abolished as a concept.
Natural resources became shared.

00:09:43.620 --> 00:09:49.370
Language was unified, and religion
and weapons were removed

00:09:49.370 --> 00:09:51.950
as the cause of conflict.

00:09:51.950 --> 00:09:58.540
Humanity finally found peace through
moving and resetting the world.

00:09:58.540 --> 00:10:02.120
It's starting to become the history we know.

00:10:02.120 --> 00:10:05.660
The great move took place over four years.

00:10:05.660 --> 00:10:10.830
On July 5th, 2057, shortly after
the move was completed,

00:10:10.830 --> 00:10:14.700
the asteroid struck as expected.

00:10:14.700 --> 00:10:19.410
When things started to get on track,
the world government was established.

00:10:19.410 --> 00:10:23.910
The first thing they did was
shut down all wormholes forever.

00:10:23.910 --> 00:10:26.120
Shut down forever...

00:10:26.120 --> 00:10:31.450
A rational choice.
It's a requirement to ensure peace.

00:10:31.450 --> 00:10:36.160
All existing wormholes were destroyed,
along with the technologies behind them.

00:10:36.160 --> 00:10:43.450
The ones who took on the job was
Vix Industries, who made the wormholes.

00:10:43.450 --> 00:10:46.160
The predecessor to the royal family.

00:10:46.160 --> 00:10:51.660
The political power they gained from this
allowed Vix to create the Royal Quarter.

00:10:51.660 --> 00:10:54.410
What about the wormhole you used?

00:10:54.410 --> 00:10:59.450
The Vix maintained one wormhole in secret.

00:10:59.450 --> 00:11:03.500
Wait, but if the wormholes
were removed from history...

00:11:03.500 --> 00:11:04.500
Yes.

00:11:04.500 --> 00:11:06.750
How would anyone explain
how the move took place?

00:11:06.750 --> 00:11:12.000
Yes. The wormhole is required
to explain how it all worked out.

00:11:12.000 --> 00:11:16.000
That's why they removed
the immigration itself from history.

00:11:16.000 --> 00:11:17.330
What...?

00:11:17.330 --> 00:11:21.910
There was no planetary immigration.
They created a false history.

00:11:21.910 --> 00:11:25.910
That's impossible! How could they possibly
wipe history so cleanly?!

00:11:25.910 --> 00:11:28.200
You said they pioneered
the planet from scratch, right?

00:11:28.200 --> 00:11:32.750
There's no way they could hide the process
of building civilization out from nothing!

00:11:32.750 --> 00:11:37.370
Besides, it doesn't make sense that
the immigration finished in 2057.

00:11:37.370 --> 00:11:39.660
It's 2063 now.

00:11:39.660 --> 00:11:43.750
There's no way we could build up to
our level of civilization in just six years.

00:11:43.750 --> 00:11:48.450
Right. Even with all the advanced tech,
it would take, at least...

00:11:48.450 --> 00:11:50.620
...100 years...

00:11:54.040 --> 00:11:57.040
I get it... I see it now.

00:11:57.040 --> 00:12:00.370
They rolled history back by 100 years.

00:12:00.370 --> 00:12:01.290
What?!

00:12:01.290 --> 00:12:03.290
What do you mean?!

00:12:03.290 --> 00:12:07.700
Our history says the world government
was established in 1963,

00:12:07.700 --> 00:12:12.870
but it was actually 2063,
early in the pioneering days.

00:12:12.870 --> 00:12:16.000
So they rolled it back by 100 years
to let civilization catch back up.

00:12:16.000 --> 00:12:19.620
Roll back...? But how?

00:12:19.620 --> 00:12:24.410
The government decided it, and the people
never told their children about the lie.

00:12:24.410 --> 00:12:25.450
That's all.

00:12:25.450 --> 00:12:27.200
That's impossible!

00:12:27.200 --> 00:12:30.660
But in fact, you didn't know.

00:12:30.660 --> 00:12:34.620
Your parents didn't know, and neither
did their parents before them.

00:12:34.620 --> 00:12:39.250
The only citizens who know about this are
those who experienced the actual immigration.

00:12:39.250 --> 00:12:43.500
Only a handful of people from
that generation remain today.

00:12:43.500 --> 00:12:48.450
This new history has become
the truth for humanity now.

00:12:49.750 --> 00:12:51.290
What the...?

00:12:51.290 --> 00:12:52.290
Um...

00:12:52.290 --> 00:12:59.250
In our history, 1963 is when
we had World War III, right?

00:12:59.250 --> 00:13:05.580
The world was all but destroyed,
and we united as one to rebuild our world.

00:13:05.580 --> 00:13:07.160
Could that be...?

00:13:07.160 --> 00:13:12.330
World War III is fabricated. A fictitious war.

00:13:12.330 --> 00:13:16.910
The resetting of our civilization was brought
in line with the recovery from war.

00:13:18.450 --> 00:13:22.700
There was conveniently an international
crisis 100 years prior that

00:13:22.700 --> 00:13:27.160
almost lead to nuclear war.
They used it to connect the histories.

00:13:27.160 --> 00:13:30.580
Wait. I'm starting to get confused.

00:13:30.580 --> 00:13:31.700
Me, too.

00:13:31.700 --> 00:13:33.330
So...

00:13:33.330 --> 00:13:37.120
To summarize, this is how it happened.

00:13:37.120 --> 00:13:43.500
We moved to a new planet
and shut down the wormholes.

00:13:43.500 --> 00:13:48.330
We rolled history back by 100 years,
connecting Earth's history with a new story.

00:13:48.330 --> 00:13:51.910
So... history from before
that time got wiped out?

00:13:51.910 --> 00:13:54.950
Is that... really possible?

00:13:54.950 --> 00:13:59.540
Of course it must have been very difficult.

00:13:59.540 --> 00:14:03.830
Changing electronic records was relatively easy,
but silencing people was not.

00:14:03.830 --> 00:14:08.040
Still, the new history was
accepted by the people.

00:14:08.040 --> 00:14:14.870
The first generation strictly prohibited
the truth from getting out.

00:14:14.870 --> 00:14:17.040
Everyone played along.

00:14:17.040 --> 00:14:22.580
The unification of nations and languages
was a big factor. But more than that...

00:14:22.580 --> 00:14:26.160
The first generation was determined.

00:14:26.160 --> 00:14:33.080
They got a second chance, and their desire
to clean up their foolish history won out.

00:14:33.080 --> 00:14:37.080
All in the name of peace...

00:14:37.080 --> 00:14:40.120
"Foolish history"...

00:14:40.120 --> 00:14:43.700
Sorry, Polina. That's not what I meant.

00:14:43.700 --> 00:14:45.250
No, it's okay.

00:14:45.250 --> 00:14:48.580
I understand that's what needed to be done.

00:14:48.580 --> 00:14:53.910
But... thinking about all of the things
that were erased for that cause...

00:14:55.700 --> 00:14:58.290
Not everything was completely erased.

00:14:58.290 --> 00:15:01.750
There are some records of the past
that have been kept in Vixia.

00:15:01.750 --> 00:15:05.330
Thank you. Now there's something
for me to do after going to Planet Astra.

00:15:05.330 --> 00:15:09.450
I hope I can tell everyone
about history as I know it.

00:15:09.450 --> 00:15:12.540
You weren't put on ice for nothing, am I right?

00:15:12.540 --> 00:15:13.790
Hey, Funi!

00:15:13.790 --> 00:15:15.700
It's not me, it's Beego.

00:15:15.700 --> 00:15:16.750
Oh.

00:15:16.750 --> 00:15:20.370
So the year now is 2063, right?

00:15:20.370 --> 00:15:23.790
Yes, the 100th anniversary of the world government.

00:15:23.790 --> 00:15:26.700
So the real year is...

00:15:26.700 --> 00:15:29.040
2163...?

00:15:29.040 --> 00:15:31.500
"Thump Thump"
So Polina is...

00:15:31.500 --> 00:15:37.500
This might be tough to hear, but Polina
was not asleep for 12 years, but 112.

00:15:40.160 --> 00:15:41.750
--Uh-oh. Polina got knocked out.

00:15:41.750 --> 00:15:42.950
--Hey, bring her here.
--Uh-oh. Polina got knocked out.

00:15:42.950 --> 00:15:45.790
So is Polina 140 years old?

00:15:45.790 --> 00:15:47.950
Funi, don't rub it in.

00:15:47.950 --> 00:15:50.790
One hundred forty... One hundred forty...

00:15:50.790 --> 00:15:53.290
One hundred... forty...

00:15:59.580 --> 00:16:04.660
Wow, I don't even know. Really.

00:16:04.660 --> 00:16:09.450
Who would've thought
our history was all wrong?

00:16:09.450 --> 00:16:13.620
That must be how education
works on Planet Astra.

00:16:13.620 --> 00:16:17.080
"The adults are lying"...

00:16:17.080 --> 00:16:19.160
That said, as far as this issue is concerned,

00:16:19.160 --> 00:16:22.700
adults in our generation were lied to as well.

00:16:22.700 --> 00:16:26.080
The real liars are adults
from further in the past...

00:16:26.080 --> 00:16:32.000
It's a tough call. I can't say I'm against
the idea of lying for the sake of peace.

00:16:32.000 --> 00:16:37.910
Yes. In that way, we're just like Charce.

00:16:37.910 --> 00:16:42.160
We were raised that way,
so that's how we became.

00:16:42.160 --> 00:16:46.120
But I don't think we can keep on like this.

00:16:48.370 --> 00:16:53.370
We have to look at the world
with our own eyes, minds, and doubts.

00:16:53.370 --> 00:16:58.500
I think that's what needs to be done
in order to become our true selves.

00:16:58.500 --> 00:17:02.290
Our true selves. That's heavy.

00:17:02.290 --> 00:17:04.750
This is indeed heavy.

00:17:04.750 --> 00:17:07.750
It's not something we here can think about
and come up with a conclusion by ourselves.

00:17:07.750 --> 00:17:11.620
All of the people living on Astra
need to think about it.

00:17:11.620 --> 00:17:16.040
That's why we have to make it home,
and bring this story back to them.

00:17:16.040 --> 00:17:18.040
Aye, yeah!

00:17:21.750 --> 00:17:25.330
The first issue is our originals.

00:17:25.330 --> 00:17:29.080
If they find out about us, won't they
come after us to hide the facts?

00:17:29.080 --> 00:17:30.620
Not just that.

00:17:30.620 --> 00:17:36.330
If we go back unprepared, the truth of
the wormholes and history will get out.

00:17:36.330 --> 00:17:41.540
I hear there is division in the government
for keeping the secrets hidden.

00:17:41.540 --> 00:17:44.700
Maybe they're the ones responsible
for taking out my brother.

00:17:44.700 --> 00:17:49.200
Maybe he learned about the secret of Astra,
not just about the clones.

00:17:49.200 --> 00:17:52.120
Why don't we send a message
to the media before we arrive?

00:17:52.120 --> 00:17:56.620
Once we get close to Astra, we should be able
to send a message from our handhelds.

00:17:56.620 --> 00:18:02.750
To the press? Isn't it risky to get
in touch with a big organization?

00:18:02.750 --> 00:18:05.000
If the government gets word, it's over for us.

00:18:05.000 --> 00:18:11.040
So we have to find a trustworthy person
that can make a big reveal in a way that

00:18:11.040 --> 00:18:13.540
the government can't suppress...?

00:18:13.540 --> 00:18:17.330
Do we know any adults like that...?

00:18:18.790 --> 00:18:21.080
I do, just one person.

00:18:21.080 --> 00:18:26.330
A police officer who was going after
Esposito's corruption with my brother.

00:18:26.330 --> 00:18:30.330
Lieutenant Grace, I think. He's in Mousanish.

00:18:30.330 --> 00:18:31.200
That's it!

00:18:31.200 --> 00:18:36.500
But... I don't know his contact info.
I can't look him up from here.

00:18:38.620 --> 00:18:44.910
Why don't we send a message to my mother
and get her to contact Lieutenant Grace?

00:18:44.910 --> 00:18:47.660
My mother is on our side.

00:18:47.660 --> 00:18:50.160
--Oh!
--That's a great idea!

00:18:50.160 --> 00:18:51.370
What do you think?

00:18:51.370 --> 00:18:55.330
Yeah. She raised you, right?

00:18:55.330 --> 00:18:58.200
Then she must be an honest,
kind person like you.

00:18:59.290 --> 00:19:00.910
Let's go with that plan.

00:19:00.910 --> 00:19:04.040
Um, yes, right.

00:19:05.000 --> 00:19:06.620
Good one, Captain.

00:19:06.620 --> 00:19:08.750
I'm jealous.

00:19:10.370 --> 00:19:12.500
Not as good as us, of course.

00:19:12.500 --> 00:19:14.080
Yes, indeed.

00:19:14.080 --> 00:19:15.790
Whatever...

00:19:15.790 --> 00:19:19.660
These young'uns are all about the romance!

00:19:24.790 --> 00:19:27.450
Team B5, camp log.

00:19:27.450 --> 00:19:32.870
Before arriving on Astra, we decided
to drop out of faster-than-light drive

00:19:32.870 --> 00:19:35.580
to send out a message.

00:19:35.580 --> 00:19:40.250
A single message that decides our future,
and the future of Planet Astra as a whole.

00:19:40.250 --> 00:19:43.330
The responsibility is huge.

00:19:43.330 --> 00:19:48.750
There's so much to cover here,
but since it's a message to my mother,

00:19:48.750 --> 00:19:52.290
I think I have to be the one to write it.

00:19:54.290 --> 00:19:56.700
"Space near Planet McPa
Day 139 of being lost in space"

00:19:59.290 --> 00:20:04.160
I will be sending this camp log
out with the message.

00:20:33.750 --> 00:20:38.790
Mom, we're all doing well up here!

00:20:41.290 --> 00:20:44.870
"Faster-than-light travel
Day 146 of being lost in space"

00:20:55.080 --> 00:20:59.250
We've come this far.
Now it's all up to our welcoming party.

00:20:59.250 --> 00:21:02.200
I hope our message got through.

00:21:02.200 --> 00:21:06.330
I can't take this anymore! I'm so nervous!

00:21:06.330 --> 00:21:11.830
It's okay, Quitterie. Let's trust
my mom and Sergeant Pepper.

00:21:11.830 --> 00:21:13.250
It's Lieutenant Grace!

00:21:17.870 --> 00:21:19.700
Hey, Charce.

00:21:19.700 --> 00:21:21.160
What is it?

00:21:21.160 --> 00:21:26.950
If the king can't rejuvenate anymore,
who's going to be the next king?

00:21:26.950 --> 00:21:32.790
It would be someone from
the extended Vix royal family.

00:21:32.790 --> 00:21:35.160
I have a good guess who it would be,

00:21:35.160 --> 00:21:38.250
and he's probably the one
behind Seira's assassination.

00:21:38.250 --> 00:21:42.700
Once I get back, I'm going
to investigate this, too.

00:21:42.700 --> 00:21:47.620
I'll help you. I'm trying to become a journalist.

00:21:49.160 --> 00:21:51.410
Yes...!

00:21:51.410 --> 00:21:54.830
But I guess the adventures are all over.

00:21:54.830 --> 00:21:59.870
What are you talking about? It all begins
the moment we get back to Astra.

00:21:59.870 --> 00:22:04.500
Our lives officially start
the moment we get back.

00:22:09.540 --> 00:22:10.790
What's that sound?

00:22:10.790 --> 00:22:13.370
It's a ship proximity alert.
Everyone get to the bridge.

00:22:13.370 --> 00:22:15.160
Isn't it our welcome party?

00:22:15.160 --> 00:22:16.160
I don't know yet.

00:22:16.160 --> 00:22:18.370
Or did the government find out?

00:22:44.500 --> 00:22:48.000
This is starship<i> Astra</i>, please respond.

00:22:54.500 --> 00:23:00.830
Please respond! This is starship<i> Astra</i>,
crewed by Caird High Team B5!

00:23:00.830 --> 00:23:02.250
Please respond!

00:23:14.870 --> 00:23:17.450
Did you summon me, your majesty?

00:23:17.450 --> 00:23:21.580
Mark. There is an important matter
I must discuss with you.

00:23:21.580 --> 00:23:26.580
Yes! It's finally here! The time for me
to gain the right of succession!

00:23:26.580 --> 00:23:31.790
After getting rid of Seira and getting
her clone to join the others,

00:23:31.790 --> 00:23:35.080
it's finally time for my efforts to pay off!

00:23:35.080 --> 00:23:38.410
I, Mark, am the next king!

00:23:38.410 --> 00:23:40.660
Hey, you can't just...

00:23:40.660 --> 00:23:44.160
What is it? I told you
not to let anyone in here.

00:23:45.870 --> 00:23:48.410
This is the police.

00:23:48.410 --> 00:23:53.750
You've been charged with illegal human cloning
and solicitation of murder.

00:23:53.750 --> 00:23:57.910
Murder?! Who are you suggesting I killed?!

00:23:57.910 --> 00:24:02.000
Oh, excuse me. Attempted murder.

00:24:02.000 --> 00:24:03.660
Attempted?

00:24:03.660 --> 00:24:09.120
We received a message from individuals
claiming to be the missing Caird High kids.

00:24:09.120 --> 00:24:14.160
We reviewed their claims and photos,
and confirmed that all of Team B5 are alive.

00:24:14.160 --> 00:24:15.330
Impossible!

00:24:15.330 --> 00:24:19.200
I can tell from your reaction
that you understand everything.

00:24:19.200 --> 00:24:25.540
You have no authority over us.
Please follow us to the precinct.

00:24:25.540 --> 00:24:27.410
Charce...

00:24:31.120 --> 00:24:34.950
Oh, are you Mark Vix?

00:24:34.950 --> 00:24:40.080
We need to ask you a few questions, too,
about the princess's murder.

00:24:48.410 --> 00:24:52.330
Lieutenant Grace, what's going
on in this Vixia area...?

00:24:52.330 --> 00:24:58.080
A big box of secrets. The king is
the defender of the lock, I guess.

00:24:58.080 --> 00:25:00.750
But that won't last much longer.

00:25:00.750 --> 00:25:04.830
The secret will come out of the box,
and our world will return to chaos.

00:25:04.830 --> 00:25:09.290
I must say, though, I think that's
a healthier world overall.

00:25:09.290 --> 00:25:12.370
I'm sorry, I'm afraid I don't understand...

00:25:12.370 --> 00:25:17.790
Yeah, you'll see soon. This is going
to turn the world upside down.

00:25:19.080 --> 00:25:25.080
This is starship <i>Astra</i>, crewed by
Caird High Team B5. Please respond!

00:25:30.700 --> 00:25:34.080
Can you hear us, starship <i>Astra</i>? Respond.

00:25:34.080 --> 00:25:36.910
This is starship <i>Astra</i>. We hear you. Over.

00:25:36.910 --> 00:25:38.870
This is the Astra Planetary Government.

00:25:38.870 --> 00:25:43.040
Your originals have all
been taken into custody.

00:25:43.040 --> 00:25:46.080
Follow this ship to the surface.

00:25:46.080 --> 00:25:47.950
Welcome home, kids.

00:25:49.790 --> 00:25:53.540
Yes!

00:25:54.410 --> 00:25:57.250
"Planet Astra
Day 146 of being lost in space"

00:25:57.250 --> 00:25:59.620
"Planet Astra
Day of return"

00:26:03.120 --> 00:26:06.120
A lot of stuff sure did happen.

00:26:06.120 --> 00:26:08.200
Seriously, way too much.

00:26:08.200 --> 00:26:11.700
What do you remember the most?

00:26:11.700 --> 00:26:13.290
Let's see...

00:26:13.290 --> 00:26:18.160
For me, when the ship
almost crashed. That was close.

00:26:22.120 --> 00:26:28.290
When the ship was disabled on Icriss,
I thought we were done for.

00:26:31.160 --> 00:26:35.620
I can't forget getting a gun pointed
at my head while I stripped naked.

00:26:35.620 --> 00:26:37.790
Shut up about that already!

00:26:40.250 --> 00:26:44.250
I remember singing for everyone
on Shummoor, when you all fell ill.

00:26:48.250 --> 00:26:53.000
For me... when Captain saved me with his arm.

00:27:00.410 --> 00:27:05.200
Me, too. Kanata saved me with his arm.

00:27:05.200 --> 00:27:09.790
Me, also! Kanata held me in his arm!

00:27:11.790 --> 00:27:16.040
And me as well. I was saved by your arm.

00:27:30.160 --> 00:27:31.790
Thank you!

00:27:33.120 --> 00:27:35.040
Thanks, Kanata!

00:27:35.040 --> 00:27:36.370
Kanata!

00:27:38.200 --> 00:27:40.700
Hey, stop. Come on.

00:27:43.830 --> 00:27:47.540
It's all of us. We all worked together.

00:27:47.540 --> 00:27:52.870
We wouldn't have made it if even one
of us wasn't here. Good work.

00:27:52.870 --> 00:27:56.540
What is the most memorable moment for you?

00:27:56.540 --> 00:27:58.750
For me, now.

00:27:58.750 --> 00:28:02.160
This instant right now, our landing.

00:28:06.700 --> 00:28:08.290
Wow.

00:28:09.250 --> 00:28:12.250
It feels like I've missed
this place for such a long time.

00:28:12.250 --> 00:28:14.500
We've been to many places.

00:28:14.500 --> 00:28:16.660
Yes, but...

00:28:16.660 --> 00:28:19.830
It's prettier than any other planet.

00:28:19.830 --> 00:28:27.290
Though humanity has buried all the tunnels,
if used right, we can explore much faster.

00:28:27.290 --> 00:28:30.080
We can broaden our horizons.

00:28:30.080 --> 00:28:35.410
"We should forge on
without fear," Kanata said.

00:28:35.410 --> 00:28:41.330
Humanity did realize peace, but it's
an unnatural one, barricaded by lies.

00:28:41.330 --> 00:28:46.450
We are comfortable saying it's time
to break out of the walls and go out.

00:28:46.450 --> 00:28:51.910
There must be terrible things out there,
and lots of dangers.

00:28:51.910 --> 00:28:58.000
But we would be fine, as long as we hold
each other's hands and support each other.

00:28:58.000 --> 00:29:02.370
If we reach out into the darkness,
we should see the light.

00:29:02.370 --> 00:29:04.790
Wow! Look, so many people.

00:29:04.790 --> 00:29:06.750
They brought cameras and things.

00:29:06.750 --> 00:29:09.250
So the press did come after all.

00:29:09.250 --> 00:29:12.160
Oh, it's Mom!

00:29:12.160 --> 00:29:14.540
Hey, Mom.

00:29:14.540 --> 00:29:17.540
Guys, that was a long camp.
Good work out there.

00:29:17.540 --> 00:29:20.080
I'll see you all back at school.

00:29:20.080 --> 00:29:22.160
Aye, yeah!

00:29:23.080 --> 00:29:26.500
Overcome hardships to reach what's beyond.

00:29:26.500 --> 00:29:29.000
We are going forward.

00:29:29.000 --> 00:29:33.120
Aries Spring, team B5 camp log secretary.

00:29:36.700 --> 00:29:38.080
I'm home!

00:29:40.250 --> 00:29:47.370
Here is an update to the return of
the ten missing Caird High students.

00:29:47.370 --> 00:29:50.580
The students claim to be illegal clones,

00:29:50.580 --> 00:29:54.870
and are accusing the individuals
who created them.

00:29:54.870 --> 00:30:03.750
The police investigated this claim,
and have taken seven suspects into custody.

00:30:03.750 --> 00:30:10.290
Also, Senator Marco Esposito
is believed to be involved as well.

00:30:10.290 --> 00:30:13.080
The police plan to bring him in for questioning.

00:30:13.080 --> 00:30:18.790
Here is the interview that took
place today with the students.

00:30:18.790 --> 00:30:20.290
Injuries?

00:30:20.290 --> 00:30:23.120
Injuries... Well...

00:30:23.120 --> 00:30:28.450
My arm got blown away, I guess.

00:30:28.450 --> 00:30:34.500
But in the end, that also turned into
a "who can make the funniest arm" game.

00:30:34.500 --> 00:30:38.870
Oh, the winner was the arm made
of a three-pronged crayfish claw.

00:30:38.870 --> 00:30:41.910
I got high marks for making
the claws actually move.

00:30:41.910 --> 00:30:44.250
You shouldn't have won that one!

00:30:44.250 --> 00:30:48.370
I think many people are curious
about the food issues.

00:30:48.370 --> 00:30:51.620
I'm sure you had to fight
starvation and dehydration.

00:30:51.620 --> 00:30:56.080
Tell us about the troubles you must have had.

00:30:56.080 --> 00:30:57.830
Yunhua, tell them.

00:30:57.830 --> 00:31:00.790
Aries, you should tell them.

00:31:00.790 --> 00:31:02.540
Um...

00:31:04.120 --> 00:31:06.870
I gained two kilos.

00:31:08.700 --> 00:31:11.000
Just one more question, please!

00:31:11.000 --> 00:31:16.410
Good work, guys. To avoid any issues,
you'll be staying at a hotel we prepared.

00:31:16.410 --> 00:31:17.750
Yay!

00:31:17.750 --> 00:31:22.120
What happens to our starship <i>Astra</i>?

00:31:22.120 --> 00:31:26.750
It's a precious relic of the past.
A museum already contacted us about it.

00:31:26.750 --> 00:31:29.160
A museum...

00:31:38.120 --> 00:31:42.540
Our dramatic return was reported
all over the world.

00:31:42.540 --> 00:31:46.080
People were surprised by how
much fun we made the trip sound.

00:31:46.080 --> 00:31:50.750
We were pulled into interviews
with every media outlet,

00:31:50.750 --> 00:31:54.040
and appeared on television almost every day.

00:31:54.040 --> 00:31:57.450
Also, about the secret of the world.

00:31:57.450 --> 00:32:01.540
Kanata and Charce attended many
meetings with government officials,

00:32:01.540 --> 00:32:04.410
and insisted that we must
release the truth now.

00:32:04.410 --> 00:32:08.700
In fact, several scholars and journalists
had already been catching on.

00:32:08.700 --> 00:32:13.620
When Kanata said he would release the truth
with or without the government's help,

00:32:13.620 --> 00:32:19.290
they decided to officially release
all of the hidden facts to the public.

00:32:19.290 --> 00:32:23.080
Of course, this was followed by a huge uproar,

00:32:23.080 --> 00:32:27.950
and there was a rise in anti-government
protests in some areas.

00:32:27.950 --> 00:32:31.950
What helped calm that down, though,

00:32:31.950 --> 00:32:37.040
was Kanata's book,
<i>The Adventure of the Spaceship Astra</i>.

00:32:37.040 --> 00:32:43.660
The entire trip was covered in a humorous tone
and the book became a best seller.

00:32:43.660 --> 00:32:48.000
The final chapter talked about how you
must see the world with your own eyes.

00:32:48.000 --> 00:32:54.200
This resonated with people all over the world,
which directed the chaotic energy

00:32:54.200 --> 00:32:58.200
towards learning about the truth
and vowing to uphold peace.

00:32:58.200 --> 00:33:03.000
Quitterie jumped on the bandwagon
to become a model in a fashion magazine.

00:33:03.000 --> 00:33:04.910
You have a problem with that?

00:33:04.910 --> 00:33:07.790
But Charce ended up
becoming the most popular.

00:33:07.790 --> 00:33:09.450
What's with this guy?!

00:33:11.540 --> 00:33:15.580
Oh, about what happened to Charce?

00:33:18.080 --> 00:33:22.000
Charce was never charged with a crime
because he was determined to have been

00:33:22.000 --> 00:33:28.040
in a deeply brainwashed state at the time,
and because none of us pressed charges.

00:33:28.040 --> 00:33:30.750
After that, a lot of things happened.

00:33:30.750 --> 00:33:33.700
Really, a lot of things...

00:33:33.700 --> 00:33:38.450
And later, he became king of Vixia.

00:33:39.700 --> 00:33:43.580
After taking up the throne,
Charce immediately gave up all political power.

00:33:43.580 --> 00:33:48.540
He released all of the secrets held by
the royal family, including the wormhole,

00:33:48.540 --> 00:33:50.910
for historical study.

00:33:50.910 --> 00:33:52.750
He opened parts of the castle up too,

00:33:52.750 --> 00:33:55.910
and the walls around the noble area
were taken down as well.

00:33:55.910 --> 00:34:00.500
I guess that was Charce's way
of taking responsibility.

00:34:00.500 --> 00:34:05.500
The young king's reforms got the public's
attention, making him even more popular.

00:34:05.500 --> 00:34:07.120
Enough already!

00:34:07.120 --> 00:34:13.330
So, although the days were far from calm,
we started to gain back our normal lives.

00:34:13.330 --> 00:34:14.700
Aries!

00:34:30.870 --> 00:34:34.620
We all graduated safely from Caird High,

00:34:34.620 --> 00:34:38.620
and moved on to pursue our own paths.

00:34:51.000 --> 00:34:54.620
"Planet Astra
Seven years after returning"

00:35:01.250 --> 00:35:03.250
It's you...

00:35:03.250 --> 00:35:05.620
...Ulgar...

00:35:05.620 --> 00:35:09.040
You have no right to visit me, clone.

00:35:09.040 --> 00:35:14.080
All of us Team B5 members
received updated birth certificates.

00:35:14.080 --> 00:35:16.330
You and I aren't related anymore, not family.

00:35:16.330 --> 00:35:18.910
You've grown much taller.

00:35:18.910 --> 00:35:21.870
You're beginning to resemble my son.

00:35:21.870 --> 00:35:27.160
That's what I wanted to ask you about.
Finn Zweig, my brother.

00:35:27.160 --> 00:35:31.910
Marco Esposito got him killed, right?

00:35:35.120 --> 00:35:37.660
Finn was very good at what he did.

00:35:37.660 --> 00:35:42.540
He traced our connection back to
the secrets of Vixia royalty.

00:35:42.540 --> 00:35:46.410
He was getting too close. If not Marco,
someone else would have taken him out.

00:35:46.410 --> 00:35:49.040
So you were okay with that?

00:35:49.040 --> 00:35:51.540
When he died, you were sad too!

00:35:51.540 --> 00:35:55.250
I wished you had died instead of my son.

00:35:55.250 --> 00:35:59.000
I still do.

00:35:59.000 --> 00:36:01.660
But my son is dead.

00:36:01.660 --> 00:36:04.580
If I had ended our project too, I gained nothing.

00:36:04.580 --> 00:36:10.120
I needed to complete the project,
for my son's sake, too.

00:36:10.120 --> 00:36:13.250
That was what I thought at the time.

00:36:13.250 --> 00:36:16.450
And after all that, the project failed,
and you also failed to erase us.

00:36:24.330 --> 00:36:25.790
He was...

00:36:25.790 --> 00:36:28.290
Finn was very good.

00:36:28.290 --> 00:36:30.250
He was a good son.

00:36:30.250 --> 00:36:32.370
Yeah...

00:36:32.370 --> 00:36:33.910
I know.

00:36:40.790 --> 00:36:43.080
If only...

00:36:43.080 --> 00:36:48.660
If only that old ship had not been
at the exit of the wormhole...

00:36:58.290 --> 00:37:00.330
Old ship...

00:37:05.040 --> 00:37:06.750
True.

00:37:12.160 --> 00:37:13.620
Bye, then.

00:37:25.370 --> 00:37:27.200
Hey, Polina!

00:37:27.200 --> 00:37:31.500
I'm your teacher now, you know.
Though part-time.

00:37:31.500 --> 00:37:33.790
Yes, Miss Livinskaya!

00:37:33.790 --> 00:37:35.950
Heading out now, Funi?

00:37:35.950 --> 00:37:38.950
Yes. You too, right?

00:37:38.950 --> 00:37:39.950
Yes.

00:37:39.950 --> 00:37:45.160
I have an interview now, then I'm giving
a presentation about history in a university.

00:37:45.160 --> 00:37:47.870
Seems like you ended up
becoming the busiest.

00:37:47.870 --> 00:37:49.200
Look, that's Miss Polina!

00:37:49.200 --> 00:37:51.950
I'm a precious witness of the old era.

00:37:51.950 --> 00:37:53.450
You're not 147 years old for nothing!

00:37:53.450 --> 00:37:56.000
I'm 36!

00:37:56.000 --> 00:37:58.790
You're going to Yunhua's concert tonight, right?

00:37:58.790 --> 00:38:00.660
Yes, that's where I'm headed.

00:38:00.660 --> 00:38:06.120
I wish I could go, too. Tell everyone I said hi.

00:38:06.120 --> 00:38:09.950
Hey, Ulgar!

00:38:09.950 --> 00:38:11.410
Hey, you two.

00:38:11.410 --> 00:38:14.870
Did you come pick me up?
You're going to the concert too, right?

00:38:14.870 --> 00:38:16.500
Unfortunately, I've got work.

00:38:16.500 --> 00:38:19.080
Oh, I guess journalists are busy too.

00:38:19.080 --> 00:38:22.040
Well Mr. Reporter, thank you for your escort.

00:38:22.040 --> 00:38:23.160
Aye, yeah.

00:38:23.160 --> 00:38:26.910
Wait, Ulgar is interviewing Polina?

00:38:26.910 --> 00:38:31.120
I'm jealous! It's a date!

00:38:31.120 --> 00:38:32.540
Later.

00:38:33.370 --> 00:38:36.410
I want to get a ride in your car, too!

00:38:40.290 --> 00:38:42.410
Yeah, soon.

00:38:48.120 --> 00:38:49.700
What's so funny?

00:38:49.700 --> 00:38:54.000
She looks way too much like Quitterie.

00:38:54.000 --> 00:38:57.370
I guess she's the same age now
as Quitterie was then.

00:38:57.370 --> 00:39:02.370
By the way, Yunhua's concert is important,
too, but what about the spaceport?

00:39:02.370 --> 00:39:03.870
Aren't they leaving soon?

00:39:03.870 --> 00:39:08.450
Actually, I stopped by the spaceport already,
and said my farewells.

00:39:08.450 --> 00:39:10.450
Oh, I see.

00:39:10.450 --> 00:39:16.540
I couldn't see the captain,
but I'm sure he'll be back soon.

00:39:16.540 --> 00:39:18.750
Perhaps he will need to be
interviewed soon, too.

00:39:19.620 --> 00:39:22.250
"Earth Memorial Hall
Prior to Yunhua’s concert"

00:39:22.700 --> 00:39:25.790
Like I said, Yunhua is our friend!

00:39:25.790 --> 00:39:28.870
Don't you know about us? We're Team B5!

00:39:28.870 --> 00:39:32.370
It's okay, Quitterie.
We don't have to go backstage now.

00:39:32.370 --> 00:39:34.910
We can see her after the show.

00:39:34.910 --> 00:39:37.500
So we're just waiting for Funi, right?

00:39:37.500 --> 00:39:38.790
What about Ulgar?

00:39:38.790 --> 00:39:41.830
He's flying around all over the place
and rarely goes home.

00:39:41.830 --> 00:39:44.410
Last night he came to crash at my place.

00:39:44.410 --> 00:39:47.750
Don't worry about that busy bee.

00:39:47.750 --> 00:39:52.290
Speaking of flying around,
aren't they taking off today?

00:39:52.290 --> 00:39:55.580
They told us not to go to send them off,
but aren't you worried?

00:39:55.580 --> 00:40:00.790
Of course not! If he wants to leave his
pretty wife behind, it must be important.

00:40:00.790 --> 00:40:03.500
Oh, so you're angry.

00:40:03.500 --> 00:40:05.370
Aries, you can be upset too.

00:40:05.370 --> 00:40:06.370
Yes.

00:40:06.370 --> 00:40:08.870
Is everything okay with you two?

00:40:08.870 --> 00:40:11.000
Well...

00:40:11.000 --> 00:40:14.870
Actually, Kanata and I are getting married.

00:40:16.450 --> 00:40:20.580
I'm sorry I didn't update you.

00:40:20.580 --> 00:40:22.160
Congratulations!

00:40:22.160 --> 00:40:24.330
Your dream finally came true!

00:40:24.330 --> 00:40:26.830
That guy made you wait way too long.

00:40:26.830 --> 00:40:31.660
He never really had a day to settle down,
preparing to become an explorer.

00:40:31.660 --> 00:40:39.540
So the two of us went to Vixia the other day,
just to do the customary thing.

00:40:42.290 --> 00:40:46.080
He asked Charce if he could
marry his daughter.

00:41:00.120 --> 00:41:03.200
When he gets back, we're throwing
the biggest ceremony!

00:41:03.200 --> 00:41:06.290
Aries, you mentioned you wanted
a baby soon, right?

00:41:06.290 --> 00:41:09.660
Yes. I want a girl.

00:41:09.660 --> 00:41:11.120
Her name will be...

00:41:11.120 --> 00:41:12.410
...Seira.

00:41:17.790 --> 00:41:23.410
Thank you. Next, I'd like to sing a new song.

00:41:23.410 --> 00:41:27.700
This one is dedicated to my companions.

00:41:27.700 --> 00:41:33.950
Today, several of my precious friends
are going up into space again.

00:41:33.950 --> 00:41:39.330
I remember that five-month long trip
from when I was 17 years old.

00:41:39.330 --> 00:41:43.250
That was a precious moment of my youth.

00:41:43.250 --> 00:41:50.000
We worked together to reach our goal,
desperately, and moved forward.

00:41:50.000 --> 00:41:53.750
I was trapped in a shell,
unable to express myself.

00:41:53.750 --> 00:41:57.540
I am who I am thanks to them.

00:42:01.450 --> 00:42:05.830
I will never forget those adventures.

00:42:06.620 --> 00:42:13.370
We went through so many dangers,
fought each other, cried, got depressed...

00:42:13.370 --> 00:42:19.040
A lot happened, but what I always
remember first is how we all smiled.

00:42:19.040 --> 00:42:26.160
The captain made a fortune with his book
and bought back that old ship.

00:42:26.160 --> 00:42:33.660
I understand how he feels.
That ship represents our friendship.

00:42:33.660 --> 00:42:37.830
Our journey continues,
for years and years to come.

00:42:37.830 --> 00:42:42.540
The <i>Astra </i>will... The <i>Astra </i>will move on!

00:42:42.540 --> 00:42:46.330
Please listen. "The Adventure
of the Spaceship Astra."

00:43:04.410 --> 00:43:07.660
"Mousanish Spaceport
Day of departure"

00:43:14.580 --> 00:43:20.540
Hey, are you sure our ship is okay?
It looks a lot older than the others.

00:43:20.540 --> 00:43:23.950
The Ark series is over 100 years old.
It's almost a fossil.

00:43:23.950 --> 00:43:31.040
But don't worry. I've personally applied
the perfect maintenance to the interior.

00:43:31.040 --> 00:43:36.000
Besides, you know how it feels
to travel on that ship, right?

00:43:37.410 --> 00:43:38.660
Yeah.

00:43:38.660 --> 00:43:40.830
It's our ship, after all.

00:43:40.830 --> 00:43:45.790
I'm impressed. You really did get
your own ship in just seven years.

00:43:45.790 --> 00:43:48.080
How's the new prosthetic arm?

00:43:48.080 --> 00:43:52.410
You stuffed too many features in this thing.
Who needs an earpick?

00:43:52.410 --> 00:43:53.080
But anyway...

00:43:53.080 --> 00:43:54.370
Not anyway!

00:43:54.370 --> 00:44:00.580
Our mission is to scout out potential
candidates to place wormhole exits.

00:44:00.580 --> 00:44:05.950
We'll go to McPa first, and use the wormhole
there to go towards Gazenette.

00:44:05.950 --> 00:44:11.000
And beyond that, the unknown. Nice.

00:44:11.000 --> 00:44:14.620
By the way, Ulgar came by.

00:44:14.620 --> 00:44:16.450
Seriously? You didn't invite him?

00:44:16.450 --> 00:44:17.830
I did.

00:44:17.830 --> 00:44:22.040
He said, "No, I'm afraid the captain
will lead us to get lost in space again."

00:44:22.040 --> 00:44:23.700
What?!

00:44:23.700 --> 00:44:26.330
He hasn't changed, has he?

00:44:26.330 --> 00:44:28.250
Hey, is that...?

00:44:28.250 --> 00:44:29.250
Huh?

00:44:30.330 --> 00:44:31.750
Hey, sorry I'm late.

00:44:31.750 --> 00:44:33.450
Charce!

00:44:33.450 --> 00:44:35.370
What are you doing here?!

00:44:35.370 --> 00:44:37.450
Well, I did RSVP "will be there if I can."

00:44:37.450 --> 00:44:41.750
This isn't a party! And is it okay for
the king to go off adventuring?!

00:44:41.750 --> 00:44:45.250
But I promised...

00:44:45.250 --> 00:44:47.700
...that I'm going to be your right-hand man.

00:44:49.290 --> 00:44:51.660
That was a joke.

00:44:51.660 --> 00:44:54.620
At any rate, I'm more useful than Kanata.

00:44:54.620 --> 00:44:56.870
What? I'm going to launch
missiles from my elbow.

00:44:56.870 --> 00:44:57.700
That's not a feature.

00:44:57.700 --> 00:44:58.750
That should have been a feature!

00:44:58.750 --> 00:45:01.040
--Add it yourself then.
--I will then!

00:45:12.250 --> 00:45:14.250
Hey. What's wrong?

00:45:14.250 --> 00:45:16.580
Let's go, Captain.

00:45:16.580 --> 00:45:18.160
Aye, yeah.

00:45:28.040 --> 00:45:32.580
We've finally made it this far, guys...

00:45:39.040 --> 00:45:40.950
<i>Astra</i>, take off!

00:45:40.950 --> 00:45:42.450
Aye, yeah!

00:45:58.870 --> 00:46:00.410
Destination!

00:46:02.160 --> 00:46:03.830
The unknown.

00:46:16.250 --> 00:46:18.330
To the far reaches of space!
